proof.text:
Write $\varphi_r=\varphi^{[r]}$. By [lem-trf-iterated-weil-cocycle], Step 8, and naturality of transport [def-weil-frobenius-cohomology-transport] at $\varphi_n:G_nK\to K$,
$$
\begin{aligned}
H(\varphi_{m+n})\tau_{m+n,K}
&=H(\varphi_m)H(G_m\varphi_n)\tau_{m,G_nK}\tau_{n,K}\\
&=H(\varphi_m)\tau_{m,K}H(\varphi_n)\tau_{n,K}.
\end{aligned}
$$
The compact-description formula [lem-trf-frobenius-operator-compact-description] identifies this with $F_{c,K}^{m+n}=F_{c,K}^mF_{c,K}^n$. Setting $m=1$ and inducting from $n=1$ gives precisely the powers of the one-step operator. Together with Step 7 this proves the global cocycle compatibility.

For the scheme coefficient maps, multiplicativity of [prop-trf-scheme-galois-comparison] reads $\kappa_{m+n,K}=G_m(\kappa_{n,K})\kappa_{m,P_nK}$. Write $u_r=\varphi_r\kappa_{r,K}$ as in [def-trf-iterated-weil-map]. Naturality of $\kappa_m$ at $u_n:P_nK\to K$ and [lem-trf-iterated-weil-cocycle] give
$$
\begin{aligned}
u_mP_m(u_n)&=\varphi_m\kappa_{m,K}P_m(u_n)
=\varphi_mG_m(u_n)\kappa_{m,P_nK}\\
&=\varphi_mG_m(\varphi_n)G_m(\kappa_{n,K})\kappa_{m,P_nK}
=\varphi_{m+n}\kappa_{m+n,K}=u_{m+n}.
\end{aligned}
$$
All domains use the canonical identifications of [lem-weil-pbc-proetale-derived-pullback-composition]. This is the scheme-side cocycle asserted in the statement.
